Kubernetes Monitoring Stack (Prometheus + Grafana + Loki) – Setup & Troubleshooting Guide
🔧 1. Install kube-prometheus-stack
helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update

helm install monitoring prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack -n monitoring --create-namespace
🔍 2. Verify Installation
kubectl get pods -n monitoring

✅ Expected:

Prometheus → Running

Grafana → Running

Alertmanager → Running

🌐 3. Access Grafana
Get password
kubectl get secret -n monitoring monitoring-grafana \
-o jsonpath="{.data.admin-password}" | base64 -d
Port forward
kubectl port-forward svc/monitoring-grafana 3000:80 -n monitoring

👉 Open: http://localhost:3000
👉 Username: admin

🌍 4. Expose Grafana via NodePort (Optional)
grafana:
  service:
    type: NodePort
    nodePort: 30000

Apply via Helm upgrade.

⚠️ COMMON ISSUE: Grafana CrashLoopBackOff
Error:
Only one datasource per organization can be marked as default
Fix:

Edit datasource config

Ensure ONLY ONE:

isDefault: true
📦 5. Install Loki (Correct Way)
Create values file: loki-values.yaml
deploymentMode: SingleBinary

singleBinary:
  replicas: 1

backend:
  replicas: 0

read:
  replicas: 0

write:
  replicas: 0

gateway:
  enabled: false

chunksCache:
  enabled: false

resultsCache:
  enabled: false

loki:
  auth_enabled: false
  commonConfig:
    replication_factor: 1

  storage:
    type: filesystem

  schemaConfig:
    configs:
      - from: "2024-01-01"
        store: tsdb
        object_store: filesystem
        schema: v13
        index:
          prefix: index_
          period: 24h

persistence:
  enabled: true
  size: 10Gi
  storageClassName: local-path
Install Loki
helm repo add grafana https://grafana.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update

helm install loki grafana/loki -n monitoring -f loki-values.yaml
🔍 6. Verify Loki
kubectl get pods -n monitoring | grep loki

✅ Expected:

loki-0   1/1 Running
⚠️ COMMON ISSUE: Loki Pod Pending
Check PVC:
kubectl get pvc -n monitoring
If Pending ❌

Fix StorageClass:

kubectl get storageclass
kubectl patch storageclass local-path \
-p '{"metadata": {"annotations":{"storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class":"true"}}}'

Then reinstall Loki.

⚠️ COMMON ISSUE: Loki CrashLoopBackOff
Error:

schema v11 / v13 mismatch

structured metadata error

Fix:

Use:

store: tsdb
schema: v13
🔗 7. Connect Loki to Grafana

Go to:

👉 Grafana → Data Sources → Add Loki

Use:
http://loki.monitoring.svc.cluster.local:3100

❌ Do NOT use:

http://localhost:3100
✅ Test Connection

Click:
👉 Save & Test

Expected:

Data source successfully connected
📜 8. View Logs

Go to:

👉 Explore → Select Loki

Run:

{}
⚠️ If NO logs appear

👉 Loki is working but no log collector installed.

🚀 9. Install Promtail (Log Collector)
helm install promtail grafana/promtail -n monitoring \
  --set "loki.serviceName=loki"
🔍 10. Verify Logs
{job="varlogs"}

✅ You should now see:

Pod logs

Container logs

🧠 Troubleshooting Summary
Problem	Cause	Fix
Grafana CrashLoop	Multiple default datasources	Keep only one default
Loki Pending	PVC not bound	Fix StorageClass
Loki CrashLoop	Wrong schema	Use tsdb + v13
No logs	Promtail missing	Install Promtail
Loki not reachable	Wrong URL	Use cluster DNS
🎯 Final Architecture

Prometheus → Metrics

Grafana → Dashboards

Loki → Logs

Promtail → Log collection

✅ DONE

You now have a production-ready monitoring + logging system.
